# Email for the site's forms — enquiry, mix & master order, release upload. They
# post to the /api/send route handler, which sends through Resend (https://resend.com).
# ONE key covers all three Nightfall inboxes — the route picks the inbox from the form:
#   enquiry + mix (questions, briefs, mix orders) → admin@nightfallworldwide.com
#   studio (session + WhiteWall bookings)         → studio@nightfallworldwide.com
#   upload (release uploads)                      → distribution@nightfallworldwide.com
# (mapping: `formInbox` in src/lib/content/forms.ts). Without a key the route
# answers 503 and each form opens a pre-filled email to the right inbox instead.
#
# Server-side only — no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, it must never reach the browser.
# Locally: .env for `next dev`, .dev.vars for `opennextjs-cloudflare preview`.
# Production: Cloudflare dashboard → Workers & Pages → nightfallworldwide →
# Settings → Variables and Secrets → add RESEND_API_KEY with type *Secret*
# (or from this folder: `npx wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY`).
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Sender. Its domain must be verified in Resend (Domains → Add domain →
# nightfallworldwide.com → add the DNS records it lists → Verify). The mailbox
# itself needn't exist — replies go to whoever filled in the form (Reply-To).
# RESEND_FROM=Nightfall Worldwide <website@nightfallworldwide.com>
# Testing only: send every form to one address. Until the domain is verified,
# Resend will only deliver to the account owner's own email, so point it there.
# RESEND_TO_OVERRIDE=you@example.com

# Optional — a Spotify app's credentials (free: developer.spotify.com → Dashboard →
# Create app; any name and redirect URI). With them, `npm run releases` matches every
# release in the Latest releases feed to its Spotify page by barcode. Only the sync
# script reads these — they never reach the browser. For the six-hourly sync on
# GitHub, add them as repository secrets with the same names.
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=…
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=…
